     "bilateral relations"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "India has several neighbours: Pakistan, China, Nepal, Bhutan, Bangladesh, Myanmar, Sri Lanka and the Maldives. Relations include trade, culture and sometimes border disputes. India works for peaceful solutions.\nSAARC, formed in 1985, is the South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation. India also joins groups like BRICS, the G20 and the Commonwealth, and plays a role in the UN, including in peacekeeping.\nIndia's relations with big powers like the USA, Russia and the European Union matter for trade, defence and technology. India also helps other countries through aid and education."
    }
